{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_kzc4lvfff36bnl6763bjcby5dlqhsi4pgpu354ctcuywp7lhpopq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The threshold construction collapses to the same answer via both paths — it doesn't discriminate. Let me rebuild it around a simplex that actually survives `c23`:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1197,"cache_read_input_tokens":314360,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1197,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51af6bd4-da19-4276-bde1-7f5d951f391d","uuid":"89048353-a9be-4374-9690-7f7c947d8a2e","timestamp":"2026-08-27T10:08:20.943Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_kzc4lvfff36bnl6763bjcby5dlqhsi4pgpu354ctcuywp7lhpopq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Gc2aeMsR9R1tXj3uYeZcCK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport re\np='tests/errors.rs'; s=open(p).read()\nstart = s.index('/// Row 37 — the `metric < -1.0e8f` half of the guard')\nend   = s.index('// ===========================================================================\\n// Rows 40, 41, 43, 45')\nnew = r'''/// Row 37 — the `metric < -1.0e8f` half of the guard, driven to the threshold\n/// **exactly**.\n///\n/// This is the only comparison in the library whose `<` vs `<=` distinction\n/// needs an input that lands precisely on a constant, and it is guarded by\n/// `metric`, the *freshly computed* simplex metric — not `cache->metric`. So the\n/// test has to manufacture a warm 3-simplex whose `c2Det2` is exactly `-1.0e8f`\n/// AND whose warm/cold trajectories actually diverge.\n///\n/// Construction (identity transforms throughout):\n///   * `A = AABB{(0,0),(1,1)}`, so all four A vertices are initialised and\n///     `iA = [0,0,0]` always selects `(0,0)`.\n///   * `B = AABB{(1,1), (10001+dx, -9999)}`, whose proxy vertices are\n///     `[(1,1), (10001+dx,1), (10001+dx,-9999), (1,-9999)]`.\n///   * `iB = [0,1,3]` therefore gives simplex points\n///     `p = [(1,1), (10001+dx,1), (1,-9999)]`, hence\n///     `p1-p0 = (10000+dx, 0)` and `p2-p0 = (0,-10000)` and\n///     `metric = c2Det2(p1-p0, p2-p0) = (10000+dx) * -10000`.\n///   * `dx = 0` gives exactly `-1.0e8f`; `dx = +/-2^-10` (one ULP of 10001)\n///     gives exactly `-1.0e8f -/+ 8`, i.e. the neighbouring floats.\n///\n/// With `cache->metric = 0` the other half of the conjunction\n/// (`min_metric < 2*max_metric`) is true, so nothing short-circuits. And this\n/// triangle makes `c23` take the CA-edge arm and leave `count == 2`, so the warm\n/// start genuinely changes the iteration instead of collapsing straight back to\n/// vertex A (which is what made a naive origin-centred construction useless).\n#[test]\nfn err_gjk_cache_metric_threshold() {\n    let (c, r) = both();\n    let threshold = -1.0e8f32;\n    let ulp = f32::from_bits(1.0e-3f32.to_bits()); // placeholder, unused\n    let _ = ulp;\n\n    let a = Shape::Aabb(c2AABB {\n        min: c2v { x: 0.0, y: 0.0 },\n        max: c2v { x: 1.0, y: 1.0 },\n    });\n\n    // One ULP of 10001.0 is 2^-10.\n    let step = 0.000_976_562_5f32;\n    let dxs = [0.0f32, step, -step, 2.0 * step, -2.0 * step, 1.0, -1.0];\n\n    let mut saw_exact = false;\n    for &dx in &dxs {\n        let b = Shape::Aabb(c2AABB {\n            min: c2v { x: 1.0, y: 1.0 },\n            max: c2v { x: 10001.0 + dx, y: -9999.0 },\n        });\n\n        // Recompute the metric the way c2GJK will, using the C's own exports.\n        let p0 = c2v { x: 1.0, y: 1.0 };\n        let p1 = c2v { x: 10001.0 + dx, y: 1.0 };\n        let p2 = c2v { x: 1.0, y: -9999.0 };\n        let metric =\n            unsafe { (c.c2Det2)((c.c2Sub)(p1, p0), (c.c2Sub)(p2, p0)) };\n        if metric.to_bits() == threshold.to_bits() {\n            saw_exact = true;\n        }\n        println!(\n            \"dx={dx:e} -> metric = {metric:?} (0x{:08x}){}\",\n            metric.to_bits(),\n            if metric.to_bits() == threshold.to_bits() {\n                \"  <== exactly -1.0e8f\"\n            } else {\n                \"\"\n            }\n        );\n\n        // `metric_old = 0` keeps `min_metric < 2*max_metric` true.\n        for &old in &[0.0f32, 1.0, 5.0, -1.0, -1.0e7, FLT_MAX] {\n            let cache = c2GJKCache {\n                metric: old,\n                count: 3,\n                iA: [0, 0, 0],\n                iB: [0, 1, 3],\n                div: 1.0,\n            };\n            for ur in [0, 1] {\n                let o = GjkOpts {\n                    cache: Some(cache),\n                    use_radius: ur,\n                    ..Default::default()\n                };\n                assert_gjk_eq(\n                    &format!(\n                        \"cache metric threshold dx={dx:e} metric={metric:?} \\\n                         old={old:?} ur={ur}\"\n                    ),\n                    &call_gjk(c, &a, &b, &o),\n                    &call_gjk(r, &a, &b, &o),\n                );\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    assert!(\n        saw_exact,\n        \"construction broken: no candidate produced a computed metric of \\\n         exactly -1.0e8f, so `<` vs `<=` at lib.c:400 would be untested\"\n    );\n}\n\n'''\ns = s[:start] + new + s[end:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"replaced\")\nPY\ntimeout 600 cargo test --test errors err_gjk_cache_metric_threshold -- --nocapture 2>&1 | grep -E 'dx=|test result|panicked|MISMATCH' | head -20","description":"Rewrite threshold test with a discriminating construction"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1197,"cache_read_input_tokens":314360,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1197,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51af6bd4-da19-4276-bde1-7f5d951f391d","uuid":"4db3df91-301f-4c4c-9a97-7a94f89883ce","timestamp":"2026-08-27T10:08:42.600Z"}
