{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hqvjv7zvhbvrmt4x34orv4yzn3nmomj4fpbxg7fpu2avzn7xcqca","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All `c_src/` sources retain their original checkout timestamp — untouched. \n\nVerification complete.\n\n## What I found and fixed\n\n**The critical discovery:** `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so the reference library builds at **`-O0`** — but the Rust translation's arithmetic was derived from an **optimized** disassembly. At `-O0` GCC keeps every local in a stack slot and chooses different SSE *destination* registers, and `ADDSS`/`MULSS`/`SUBSS` return the **destination** operand's NaN. Since a NaN's sign and payload are observable in the output, **10 call sites across 8 functions were behaviourally wrong on NaN inputs**:\n\n| function | was (`-O2`-derived) | is (verified vs `-O0` objdump) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `c2Mulvs` | `mul_r` | `mul_l` — a memory operand can only be the `mulss` *source* |\n| `c2Add` | `add_l` | `add_r` |\n| `c2Dot` | `add_l(mul_l, mul_l)` | `add_r(mul_l, mul_r)` |\n| `c2Det2` | `sub_l(mul_l, mul_l)` | `sub_l(mul_r, mul_r)` |\n| `c2Mulrv`, `c2MulrvT` | folded `-x+y` into `subss` | `-O0` materialises `-a.s` via `xorps`; the `addss` dest is the *first* term |\n| `c23` (2 sums), `c2Witness` (all `den*u`), `c2L` | mixed | corrected per instruction |\n\nEach fix is annotated in `src/lib.rs` with the actual instruction at its address.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 31 vs 31, **empty diff both directions**, 0 undefined non-libc symbols. Re-checked at test time so the doc can't rot.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 87 rows, all passing; branch coverage is *asserted*, not hoped for (all 7 `c23` arms, all 3 `c22` arms, both `c2D` orientations, both radius arms).\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 69 rows. The library has **no error channel at all** (no `assert`/`return -1`/error enum — grep-verified), so the surface is switch fallthroughs, null guards, numeric guards, and 23 unchecked derefs — the latter compared by **subprocess termination signal** (all 23: SIGSEGV in both).\n- **Phase D** — both feature configurations pass, with symbol parity re-diffed per combo.\n\n**85 tests, 0 failures.**\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n1. **A trap that produced a false green.** `cargo test` does *not* rebuild the `cdylib` (integration tests `dlopen` it rather than link it), so the suite ran against a **stale `.so`** and reported green while `src/lib.rs` held an injected bug. The harness now rebuilds the library itself, and I verified cold-start correctness.\n\n2. **I mutation-tested the tests.** 59 deliberate mutations; 49 caught. I did *not* accept the 10 survivors as passes — each was proven semantics-preserving (e.g. `c23`'s `div = uBC+vBC` can't depend on operand order because that arm is guarded by `uBC > 0 && vBC > 0`, so neither operand can be NaN). This exposed 3 genuine blind spots, all closed — including two boundary guards whose naive tests were **vacuous**: GJK is self-correcting, so flipping `cache_was_read` is usually invisible. Hitting them needed an all-integer-coordinate construction that makes the computed metric exactly `W*H` independent of shape position, decoupling \"land exactly on `-1.0e8f`\" from \"make the outcome observable\".\n\n`ERRORS.md` also records the 4 input classes I **deliberately don't assert** — cases where the C reads uninitialised stack (e.g. an out-of-range `C2_TYPE` leaves `c2Proxy` untouched), where demanding a match would be demanding a coin flip — each paired with the nearest deterministic neighbour that *is* tested."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":753,"cache_read_input_tokens":395863,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":753,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51af6bd4-da19-4276-bde1-7f5d951f391d","uuid":"a6c79afd-050e-4025-9196-949a436b2944","timestamp":"2026-08-27T10:24:35.842Z"}
